---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('cairn')!;
const effectiveDate = 'August 21, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${app.name} Privacy Policy — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description={`How ${app.name} handles on-device study data, private iCloud sync, App Store purchases, and Apple system features.`}
  path={`/${app.slug}/privacy`}
  noindex={true}
  socialImage="/apps/cairn.png"
  socialImageAlt="Cairn app icon"
>
  <article class="prose container">
    <a class="back-link" href="/cairn">← {app.name}</a>
    <h1>{app.name} Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Effective: {effectiveDate}</p>

    <p>
      This policy explains how {COMPANY.name} (“we”, “us”) handles information
      in {app.name} for iPhone and iPad. {app.name} is a native Microsoft
      certification exam-prep app with bundled course and exam content.
    </p>

    <p class="callout">
      <strong>The short version.</strong> {app.name} has no account, no login, no
      developer-operated backend, no ads, no analytics SDK, and no cross-app
      tracking. The app does not send personal or usage data to {COMPANY.name}.
      Study progress stays on your device and may sync through your private
      Apple iCloud database when iCloud is available.
    </p>

    <h2>Data {COMPANY.name} collects</h2>
    <p>
      {app.name} does not collect or transmit personal information, study
      activity, diagnostics, advertising identifiers, location, contacts, or
      other device data to {COMPANY.name}. We do not use advertising, analytics,
      or tracking software.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you email us for support, we receive the information you choose to put
      in that message and use it to respond. Support correspondence is separate
      from the app, and {app.name} does not attach study data to it.
    </p>

    <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      {app.name} stores your study progress and app preferences locally using
      Apple’s SwiftData framework. Exam and course content is bundled with the
      app, so it can be read without an internet connection. {COMPANY.name} does
      not receive a copy of your local study data.
    </p>

    <h2>Private iCloud sync</h2>
    <p>
      When you are signed in to iCloud and iCloud is available, Apple’s
      SwiftData and CloudKit services may sync your progress through the private
      database associated with your Apple Account. That sync is provided and
      controlled by Apple. {COMPANY.name} does not operate a progress server and
      does not receive or store the synced data on a server we operate. If
      iCloud is unavailable, {app.name} can continue using its local store.
    </p>

    <h2>Proposed App Store purchase</h2>
    <p>
      The current build contains StoreKit support for one proposed
      non-consumable purchase called <strong>Full Exam Library</strong>, priced
      at $14.99 in the United States submission. The app version was rejected,
      the combined submission remains unresolved, and the purchase is still in
      review, so there is no public listing or public purchase availability.
      If Apple approves a later submission, the App Store will process payment
      details, refunds, Family Sharing eligibility, and restores. {COMPANY.name}
      does not receive payment-card details.
    </p>

    <h2>Notifications, widgets, Live Activities, and App Intents</h2>
    <p>
      If you enable a daily study reminder, the notification is scheduled
      locally by your device. {app.name} also makes limited on-device status
      available to its own widget and Live Activity, and provides App Intents
      for Apple system features such as Siri and Shortcuts. These features use
      Apple’s system frameworks; they do not send study data to a
      {COMPANY.name}-operated notification or analytics server. You can control
      notifications, widgets, Live Activities, and Siri or Shortcuts access in
      Apple’s device settings and system interfaces.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      {app.name} contains no third-party advertising, analytics, or tracking
      SDKs. The external services it relies on are Apple system services:
      iCloud and CloudKit for optional private sync, the App Store and StoreKit
      for purchases, and the operating-system services that provide
      notifications, widgets, Live Activities, Siri, and Shortcuts. Apple may
      process information needed to provide those services under Apple’s own
      terms and privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Local study data remains on a device until you change it or delete
      {app.name}. Deleting the app removes its local app data from that device.
      If iCloud sync was used, a synced copy may remain in your Apple Account
      until you remove {app.name}’s iCloud data through Apple’s device settings,
      where applicable. Apple controls retention of App Store purchase records
      and entitlements.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because {COMPANY.name} has no {app.name} account or progress server, there
      is no account or server-side study history for us to delete.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      {app.name} is a general study tool and is not directed to children under
      13. The app does not knowingly collect personal information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy if {app.name} or its data practices change. The
      effective date at the top of this page will identify the current version.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>. For
      help using the app, visit <a href="/cairn/support/">Cairn Support</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
